{"id":"NCT07276581","title":"A Study to Investigate Efficacy and Safety of AZD1163 in Participants With Rheumatoid Arthritis","official":"A Multicentre, Parallel-group, Phase II, Randomised, Double-blind, 4 Arm Study to Evaluate Efficacy and Safety of AZD1163 in Participants With Moderately-to-Severely Active Rheumatoid Arthritis (LaunchPAD-RA)","summary":"Phase II study in participants with moderately-to-severely active rheumatoid Arthritis (RA) to evaluate efficacy and safety of AZD1163.","conditions":["Rheumatoid Arthritis"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"AZD1163"},{"type":"OTHER","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"* Inclusion\n\n  * Diagnosed with adult-onset RA as defined by the 2010 ACR/EULAR classification criteria for at least 12 weeks prior to screening.\n  * Moderately-to-severely active RA as defined by: a. \\>= 6 swollen joints on 66SJC and \\>= 6 tender joints on 68TJC; b. CRP \\> upper limit of normal.\n  * Have a positive ACPA at screening.\n  * A history of inadequate response, or loss of response, or intolerance to: a. at least one csDMARD treatment, AND/OR b. At least one and at most 2 TNFi.\n  * A history of at least 12 weeks treatment and \\>= 4 weeks stable on a csDMARD and/or SC TNFi prior to the day of randomisation.\n* Exclusion\n\n  * History or evidence of an alternate autoimmune or other condition that could confound the diagnosis of RA. Participants with RA and secondary Sjogren's disease are eligible.\n  * Have received or planning to receive any biologic DMARDs (except for TNFi) or targeted synthetic DMARDs.","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":320,"start":"2025-12-15","pcd":"2027-11-12","upd":"2026-10-09","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","areas":["other"],"central":["AstraZeneca Clinical Study Information Center · 1-877-240-9479 · information.center@astrazeneca.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Research Site","city":"Glendale","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85306","s":"R","l